Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat: `brit for-each-ref` with Git's format atoms and
 sort keys

Lists refs with Git's default `%(objectname) %(objecttype)\t%(refname)` format,
sorted by refname, with Git's pattern rules (a prefix at a `/` boundary or an
`fnmatch` glob whose `*` does not cross `/`). `--format` implements the atoms in
real use: `refname`, `refname:short` (Git's unambiguous shortening), `objectname`,
`objectname:short`, `objecttype`, `subject`, `committerdate`,
`committerdate:short` and `committerdate:iso`, plus `%%` and `%xx`. `--sort`
takes `refname` and `committerdate`, `-` reversing, the last key primary and
refname breaking ties. Any other atom or key is refused by name before output.

The help points to `brit branch list`, Brit's own branch listing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
